{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Anti-MRSA, Antibiofilm", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Peptide design: this peptide was obtained by combining BAMP-27 residues 9-20 (KFKKLFKKLSPV) and OP-145 N-terminal fragment corresponding to residues 13-29 of human LL-37 (IGKEFKRIVERIKRFLR). Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that the sequence of this peptide shows 62% similarity to CaLL. Activity: Active against S. aureus ATCC 29213 (MIC 20 uM), E. faecalis ATCC 19433 (MIC 15 uM), S. epidermidis ATCC 12228 (MIC 10 uM), MRSA (MIC 5-10 uM), E. faecium VRE (MIC 5 uM), and Gram- E. coli ATCC 25922 (MIC 10 uM), P. aeruginosa ATCC 27853 (MIC 20 uM), A. baumannii ATCC 19606 (MIC 10 uM), K. pneumoniae ATCC 13883 (MIC 2.5 uM). Antibiofilms: S. aureus (MBEC 20 uM) and P. aeruginosa (MBEC 25 uM). Toxicity: Poor hemolysis at 100 uM (2%) (hemo.lytic) and 50% toxic concentrations HEK293 and Vero IC50 61-64 uM. Updated 7/2021", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "29910626", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Infect Drug Resist. 2018 Jun 1;11:835-847. doi: 10.2147/IDR.S166236. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP02864", "source_id": "AP02864", "source_numeric_id": "02864", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP02864", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Hybridization and antibiotic synergism as a tool for reducing the cytotoxicity of antimicrobial peptides", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
